cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use KARZOUN-X in research, cite the tagged software release and its archival DOI once available."
title: "KARZOUN-X: Resource-Aware, Safety-Gated Local AI for Autonomous Spacecraft Fault Diagnosis"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Karzoun
    given-names: Mahmoud
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-2752-7744"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mkarson1997/karzoun-x"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0-rc1
keywords:
  - spacecraft autonomy
  - local LLM
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - fault diagnosis
  - telemetry
  - safety gate
  - deep-space systems
  - communication delay
abstract: >-
  KARZOUN-X is an open research prototype investigating resource-aware local language-model reasoning,
  retrieval augmentation, telemetry anomaly detection, deterministic action constraints, delayed or
  unavailable ground communication, and auditable fault-diagnosis decision support. The repository
  contains real SMAP/MSL anomaly-detection experiments and separately labeled synthetic diagnosis,
  safety, hard-stress, communication, and resource experiments. It is not flight-qualified software.
